{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792754918,"nonce":"75TRNiitweuVKoPvKETCc//7+tc=","title":"Accept declared one-way conversions between conditional branches","message":"The LSP rejects `return (value == null ? Choice.Default : value : String)` where `value:Null\u003cChoice\u003e` and `enum abstract Choice(String) to String` with `Type mismatch: expected String, found Null\u003cChoice\u003e`. A portable session regression reproduces the same false diagnostic as ashui component size defaults. The checker only tried converting the then-branch type to the else-branch type; the available conversion points the other way. Nullable target compatibility also discarded Convertible results and nullable source compatibility excluded Abstract and GenericInstance targets.\n\nCheck conditional compatibility in either direction, preserve declared conversions through nullable wrappers, and keep rejecting unrelated String/Bool branches. The runtime regression NullableEnumConditional.hx exercises both branch orders, null and non-null values, and direct nullable abstract unwrapping. Existing abstract/generic negative tests must continue to reject undeclared conversions.\n\nEvidence before the fix: /tmp/rayzor-macro-lsp-all-final.log, package_siblings_resolve_in_static_calls_and_field_chains. Macro transport projection and nested-library discovery are separate fixes.","files":null}]}